  "notes": "USAGE:\n{起業|きぎょう} focuses on the act of founding or launching a new business. It is commonly used as a noun or with する.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {起業|きぎょう}する: to start a business\n- {起業|きぎょう}{家|か}: entrepreneur\n- {起業|きぎょう}{資金|しきん}: startup capital\n- {起業|きぎょう}{支援|しえん}: startup support\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{企業|きぎょう} means \"company\" or \"enterprise\" (an existing business entity), while {起業|きぎょう} means the act of starting a business. The two are homophones but use different kanji: {企|き} (plan) vs. {起|き} (start).",
